==Trivia==
The illustration rare print of this card forms part of a narrative illustration with {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Oddish|11}}, {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Venonat|16}}, and {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Bellsprout|18}} from the same set. In each of those cards, the featured Pokémon can be seen near {{p|Snorlax}}; this card depicts the Snorlax blocking [[Kanto]] [[Kanto Route 11|Routes 11]] and [[Kanto Route 12|12]] in Generations {{gen|I}} and {{gen|III}}, while the other three Pokémon are stuck on one side of it. Together, these cards form the {{TCGP|Genetic Apex}} expansion's "A Big Snorlax Nuisance" [[Genetic Apex (TCG Pocket)#Themed Collections|Themed Collection]].

===Origin===
*This card's standard illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Kalos Starter Set|Snorlax|26}} from the {{TCG|Kalos Starter Set}}.
*{{m|Rollout}} is a [[move]] in the [[Pokémon games]] that {{p|Snorlax}} can learn.
*This card's [[Pokédex]] entry comes from {{g|Sword}}.

